<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Floriano Peixoto</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1839–1895</span></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Floriano Peixoto was a Brazilian army marshal who served as the second President of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/brazil">Brazil</a> from 1891 to 1894, taking over when <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/deodoro-da-fonseca">Deodoro da Fonseca</a> resigned. Known as the Iron Marshal, he crushed the Federalist Revolution in the south and a naval revolt in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rio-de-janeiro">Rio de Janeiro</a>, securing the new republic. He handed power to Prudente de Morais, the first civilian president.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/floriano-peixoto.jpg" alt="Floriano Peixoto" width="320" height="479" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Governo do Brasil · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Floriano_Peixoto_(1891).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
